{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1439348-the-inflict-damage-stunt-for-thrown-attacks-doesn-t-factor-in-the-opponent-s-armor","id":1439348,"title":"The \"Inflict Damage\" Stunt for Thrown Attacks doesn't factor in the opponent's Armor?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-03-11T19:24:30-08:00","id":1439348,"title":"The \"Inflict Damage\" Stunt for Thrown Attacks doesn't factor in the opponent's Armor?","content":"Like the title says. The Success cost for the &quot;Inflict Damage&quot; Stunt for all other forms of attacks is listed as (0s + opponent\u2019s Armor), but for Thrown Attacks (P.118) it's only (0s). Is there a specific reason for this, or is it just a mistake?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1964-the-voice","name":"The Voice","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T19:26:49-08:00","id":1439349,"title":"","content":"Probably a mistake.<br /> <br /> Armor should affect the inflict Damage / Cause Injury stunt the same way for both.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T18:53:56-08:00","id":1439577,"title":"","content":"For anyone coming across this post and wondering what the official word on this question actually is, well you're in luck cuz here's the official answer to my question. And (spoiler alert!) it turns out Mateus Luz was correct.<br /> <br /> According to Origins P. 125, the &quot;Soft Armor&quot; armor Tag states that it increases the Difficulty of the &quot;Inflict Damage&quot; Stunt by 1. It doesn't specify any exceptions so it's logical to assume that it applies to all instances of that Stunt. What's more, to be a bit more specific, those other instances of the &quot;Inflict Damage&quot; Stunt that do mention Armor, should technically refer specifically to Soft Armor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1964,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1964-the-voice","user":"The Voice","date":". 03-12-2021, 09:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1964-the-voice","name":"The Voice","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}